TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Image 1","issue":"STK Simulations (Wk 4–10) is scheduled to start before STK Design (Wk 7–9), an illogical task dependency."},{"where":"Image 1","issue":"Background Research runs to Wk 8 while Mission Concept is marked complete in Wk 3, leaving the concept unsupported by later research."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"No quantified mission requirements (ground resolution, revisit time, spectral bands, coverage, lifetime) are defined to drive the design."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"'Oceans have become 30 percent more acidic' is imprecise; the commonly cited figure is a ~30% rise in hydrogen-ion concentration (pH drop ~0.1)."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"No contingency, risk, or mitigation is described for schedule slippage or STK/software access problems."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"STK is named but not justified against alternatives, and no software outputs are shown."}],"overall":"Strong, well-referenced mission concept and a clear Gantt-based plan tied to the space segment. Technical progress is thin—only tutorials and reading—and requirements remain unquantified. Presentation is professional with minor referencing and figure-caption weaknesses.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":28.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Clear, well-motivated concept: purpose (bleach detection, SST, thermal stress, bathymetry), users (marine/conservation scientists), and Australian benefit are explicit, with literature cited. However, no quantified mission requirements (resolution, revisit, coverage, orbit) are stated, so it sits at the lower end of Accomplished.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"In 2016, a bleaching killed 30 percent of the reef’s coral. In 2017, another 20 percent perished."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":21.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"Gantt chart with colour-coded progress, deadlines and per-task descriptions tied to the mission (launch, orbit, ground control, comms, EOL, STK). Week 10 review acts as a buffer, but no explicit contingency or risk provision is stated, and some task sequencing is questionable.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart. Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"The syllabus work on astrodynamics will help me to understand and design an optimal mission."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Progress to date is limited to background reading and four STK tutorials; no orbit, launch, link-budget or simulation results are presented or interpreted. This is minor work only, though it is consistent with being on track.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Logical structure, clear readable prose, consistent formatting, superscript citations matching the source list. Deductions: the Gantt lacks a numbered figure caption, and the reference list is bare URLs without titles or access dates.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue. Deadlines are indicated by red lines."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"https://www.deepreef.org/projects/48-depth-model-gbr.html"}]}]}
